Before going out, I sit in front of the laptop.
Today I make a video call with my family in Mexico.
On the screen are my parents, elder brother Diego, and younger sister Sofia.
They all sing a birthday song together.
In the background, our dog Lola also barks loudly.
I laugh and say, "Quiet Lola, you also sang enough!"
My mother asks, "Maya, did you receive that small box?"
"We sent that small box for your birthday," she says.
I reply, "Yes mother, I received it just yesterday."
"And I have opened it today morning."
There are very beautiful things in that box.
Then my mother asks, "What is your plan for the evening?"
I say, "I have invited my friends home today."
"I have never celebrated a birthday away from home before."
"But I made good friends here in Mumbai."
"So they will all come here in the evening."
My family becomes very happy hearing that.
Outside, the rain starts again.
I say 'see you later' to my family and get ready for the office.
